      "seed": 1295966390,
      "version": 1838,
      "versionNonce": 435103939,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763836958810,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reinforcement Learning in un-verifiable domains\n    => RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProblem: how we do score these *at scale* (automatically)?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRLHF approach:\n    - STEP 1: Take 1,000 prompts, get 5 rollouts, order them from best to worst (cost:     \n          5,000 scores from humans)\n    - STEP 2: Train a neural net  simulator of human preferences (\"reward model\")\n    - STEP 3: Run RL as usual, but using the simulator instead of actual humans",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reinforcement Learning in un-verifiable domains\n    => RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nProblem: how we do score these *at scale* (automatically)?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRLHF approach:\n    - STEP 1: Take 1,000 prompts, get 5 rollouts, order them from best to worst (cost:            \n          5,000 scores from humans)\n    - STEP 2: Train a neural net  simulator of human preferences (\"reward model\")\n    - STEP 3: Run RL as usual, but using the simulator instead of actual humans",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
