      "updated": 1763995566030,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The \"Psychology\" of a Stochastic Parrot",
      "fontSize": 39.54285714285655,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The \"Psychology\" of a Stochastic Parrot",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "e6Bd24TmVY7px0tlM8KDm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -194.24764986130322,
      "y": -1647.9575998812115,
      "width": 760.0336303710938,
      "height": 780,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5it",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 35464016,
      "version": 1743,
      "versionNonce": 705138091,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763995566030,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nHuman-human communication is a jointly constructed activity because it is a form of coordinated \naction between individuals, such as a speaker and a listener, who work together to achieve a \nshared understanding of a part of the world.\n\nThe text generated by an LM is not grounded in communicative intent, any model of the world, \nor any model of the reader’s state of mind.\n\nAnthroporphize a machine is a common effect in humans but we must not be fooled by the \nlinguistic capabilities and take them for what they are to better deal with their answers. \nLMs are systems for stitching together sequences of tokens observed in its vast training data, \naccording to probabilistic information about how they combine: they are stochastic parrots.\n\nA lot of useful world knowledge is stored in the parameters of the network:\n    - syntax: the formal rules and structures of language\n    - associative semantic: the meanings of ideas through their relationships with other ideas\n    - facts — Discrete pieces of information (Language Models as Knowledge Bases?)\nMore opaque is their knowledge for: \n    - reasoning patterns — Implicit logical structures\n    - procedural knowledge — How to do things: steps in algorithms, problem-solving strategies, \n        common workflows e.g. coding patterns\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn conclusion, the parameters of a LM are a muddy  token-level compression of the internet.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nHuman-human communication is a jointly constructed activity because it is a form of coordinated \naction between individuals, such as a speaker and a listener, who work together to achieve a \nshared understanding of a part of the world.\n\nThe text generated by an LM is not grounded in communicative intent, any model of the world, \nor any model of the reader’s state of mind.\n\nAnthroporphize a machine is a common effect in humans but we must not be fooled by the \nlinguistic capabilities and take them for what they are to better deal with their answers. \nLMs are systems for stitching together sequences of tokens observed in its vast training data, \naccording to probabilistic information about how they combine: they are stochastic parrots.\n\nA lot of useful world knowledge is stored in the parameters of the network:\n    - syntax: the formal rules and structures of language\n    - associative semantic: the meanings of ideas through their relationships with other ideas\n    - facts — Discrete pieces of information (Language Models as Knowledge Bases?)\nMore opaque is their knowledge for: \n    - reasoning patterns — Implicit logical structures\n    - procedural knowledge — How to do things: steps in algorithms, problem-solving strategies, \n        common workflows e.g. coding patterns\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn conclusion, the parameters of a LM are a muddy  token-level compression of the internet.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
