    {
      "id": "FHLBKUh2kf0BnZbCPUNDe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1801.6474721295563,
      "y": 112.83565569475013,
      "width": 904.2855631510411,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 372799920,
      "version": 600,
      "versionNonce": 1524281874,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763832316810,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There are limits to how much can be expected from a model whose sole training objective is\nto predict the next word from large amounts of pretraining text.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHere, the LLM ignores the intent of the request and relies instead on its natural\ninclination to autoregressively generate continuations consistent with its context.\n\nNot only a stochastic parrot can be unhelpful but often results in harmful behaviors, like \ngenerating false or toxic information.\n\nWhy? Because humans also use communication to be harmful.\n\nTo address these problems, OpenAI and all the other AI companies use additional kinds\nof training for model alignment.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There are limits to how much can be expected from a model whose sole training objective is to predict the next word from large amounts of pretraining text.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHere, the LLM ignores the intent of the request and relies instead on its natural\ninclination to autoregressively generate continuations consistent with its context.\n\nNot only a stochastic parrot can be unhelpful but often results in harmful behaviors, like \ngenerating false or toxic information.\n\nWhy? Because humans also use communication to be harmful.\n\nTo address these problems, OpenAI and all the other AI companies use additional kinds\nof training for model alignment.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
